  data: {
    LLM: "Try to win at least two comparisons. Don't put all your high cards in one set if you can split them to win two tricks.\n\nIf you have an Ace, King, and 10 of different suits, they may be better used as high cards in a 'Color' or 'Run' than as individual point cards in a weak set.\n\nDefensive Partitioning: If you have a mediocre hand, try to win the 'fourth' set (the 4-card set) as it often contains more point cards dumped by others who won early with Troys.",
